{
  "_comment": "Everything the gacha can give out. Edit this file on GitHub and the next deploy has it — no code changes. A gif is a reaction that joins the pool the kana and grammar drills draw from, and it need not be a gif: animated webp, avif, png and jpeg all work, as does a photograph. Images are filenames in this folder (put them in gifs/), a path like ../feedback/correct.gif, or a full https:// URL. Any size is fine — each deploy squeezes its own copy to the same budget, so upload the original.",
  "cost": 120,
  "_cost": "Yennies per pull.",
  "duplicateRefund": 0.4,
  "_duplicateRefund": "Fraction of the cost paid back when a pull is one you already own.",
  "draw": "uniform",
  "_draw": "'uniform' — every prize equally likely, so adding one never changes what the others were worth. 'rarity' — weighted by the table below instead. While the pool is still being filled in, uniform is the honest one; under it the rarity of a prize is only its colour, and no odds are claimed on screen.",
